            <ArticleTitle>Study of Nuclear Clustering from an Ab Initio Perspective.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>062501</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.062501</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We put forward a new ab initio approach that seamlessly bridges the structure, clustering, and reactions aspects of the nuclear quantum many-body problem. The configuration interaction technique combined with the resonating group method based on a harmonic oscillator basis allows us to treat the reaction and multiclustering dynamics in a translationally invariant way and preserve the Pauli principle. Our presentation includes studies of ^{8,10}Be and an exploration of 3α clustering in ^{12}C.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
